  "worked_solution": "First, notice that $u(t)=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-t)$ is continuous at $t=0$ and \n\n$$\nu(0)=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(u)$ is continuous at $u=1$ and $u(t)$ is continuous at $t=0,$ the function $f(u(t))$ is also continuous at $t=0.$\n\nTherefore,\n${lim}_{t\\to 0}f(u(t))=f(u(0))=f(1).$",
